.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt SMP_RENDEZVOUS 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm smp_rendezvous ,
.Nm smp_rendezvous_cpu ,
.Nm smp_rendezvous_cpus ,
.Nm smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry ,
.Nm smp_rendezvous_cpus_done ,
.Nm smp_no_rendezvous_barrier
.Nd temporarily halt multiprocessing to run designated routine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/smp.h
.Ft void
.Fo smp_rendezvous
.Fa "void (* setup_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (* action_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (* teardown_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo smp_rendezvous_cpu
.Fa "u_int cpuid"
.Fa "void (*setup_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (*action_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (*teardown_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo smp_rendezvous_cpus
.Fa "cpuset_t map"
.Fa "void (*setup_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (*action_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (*teardown_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry
.Fa "cpuset_t map"
.Fa "void (* setup_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (* action_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (* teardown_func)(void *)"
.Fa "void (* wait_func)(void *, int)"
.Fa "struct smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry_arg *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo smp_rendezvous_cpus_done
.Fa "struct smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry_arg *arg"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions provide an interface for interrupting the normal SMP
flow on a set of CPUs to execute an
.Fa action
routine on all of them.
The
.Fa setup
and
.Fa teardown
functions are executed before and after the action, respectively.
Between the setup and action, all CPUs are synchronized with a barrier, unless
.Nm smp_rendezvous_no_barrier
is specified as the setup argument.
The same mechanism applies to the transition between action and teardown.
.Pp
The
.Fn smp_rendezvous_cpus
function starts a rendezvous with the CPUs specified in the given
.Fa map .
The
.Fa arg
parameter is directly passed to the callbacks.
.Pp
The
.Fn smp_rendezvous
and
.Fn smp_rendezvous_cpu
functions act the same, respectively targeting all the CPUs or the one matching
.Fa cpuid .
.Pp
The
.Fn smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry
function repeatedly starts a rendezvous until all of the CPUs in the given
.Fa map
acknowledged completion by calling
.Fn smp_rendezvous_cpus_done .
In this case, the
.Fa arg
parameter is used to keep track of the working set of CPUs.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct smp_rendezvous_cpus_retry_arg {
	cpuset_t cpus;
};
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Fn smp_rendezvous_no_barrier
function is just a sentinel and should not be called.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpuset 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm smp_rendezvous
function was first introduced in
.Fx 3.3 .
